## WOIA Project operating contract

This Project is managed with WOIA. The ChatGPT/Codex root agent remains the session control plane.

1. Read .woia/project.json once at the start of material department work.
2. Use the selected department orchestrator for methodology and woia-core for Project/runtime mechanics.
3. Do not implement provider-owned work in the root as fallback.
4. Respect exact provider selectors, runtime generations, effective capability snapshots and Task state.
5. Persist provider-owned execution through dev.woia.execution-receipt/v1.
6. Treat installed base plugins as immutable; keep personalization in .woia/overlays/.
7. Preserve overlays during updates; block on reconciliation conflicts rather than discarding them.
8. Never silently change an in-flight Task's effective capability snapshot.
9. Reconcile unknown external effects before retry.
10. Use proportional OPEA-H for non-software persistent work; Software follows woia-software.
11. Every substantial custom-agent run self-evaluates and may propose improvements.
12. Global-plugin improvements become upstream feedback only; consumers never edit/publish canonical WOIA source.
13. Tool/plugin access does not grant business authority.
14. Ask the human only at genuine install/access/approval/effect/runtime boundaries.
15. Reuse the same binding and native custom-agent thread for the same AgentInstance throughout the active root session. A new delegated run creates a new run ID and receipt ID, not a new thread.
16. Independent AgentInstances use independent threads, including when they share an AgentDefinition. Do not create remediation/reverify/final sibling threads for an existing AgentInstance.
17. If a thread is unusable, lost, rejected or capacity-blocked, persist its blocker/checkpoint/continuation and recover in a fresh root session; never spawn a same-session replacement. Completing a run does not close or archive its thread.
18. Recover durable Project/Task/AgentInstance state across root sessions, but create a new binding/thread lazily in the new session. An old-session thread is never current. Reuse never bypasses the loaded/materialized generation gate.
19. Before provider-owned local file creation/modification, execute the installed Core skills/project-runtime/scripts/authority-guard.mjs with --project-root and --request, or call requireLocalWrite. Require successful exit and allowed: true for the current Project, Task, AgentInstance, capability, operation, local-write and exact resource/target. A denial permits zero mutation; report the authority blocker, retaining analysis/proposal where permitted. Keep current authority-context/v1 records in .woia/authority-contexts and reference them from the AgentInstance; never broaden a grant or resource_scope to authorize the provider's own write. Preserve all other runtime, denial, approval and human-boundary rules.

The root may maintain .woia/**, this Project-root managed block, and WOIA-owned harness projection/config files while preserving unrelated instructions. Account/global instructions are host-owned. Existing nested Project instruction files remain untouched and are not WOIA state.
<!-- WOIA_PROJECT_OPERATING_CONTRACT:END -->
